  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_11f932f6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a photo of Michelle Obama with a photo of a person in a primate mask, both labeled with salary comparisons for personal stylist and makeup artist roles. The bottom text reads 'i can't tell the difference,' implying that Michelle Obama is indistinguishable from a monkey. This visual and textual combination is a direct and offensive racial stereotype, specifically comparing Black people to primates, which is a well-documented form of anti-Black racism. The intent is to demean Michelle Obama and, by extension, Black people, by suggesting her appearance is so 'animal-like' that she is indistinguishable from a primate, thereby dehumanizing her and reinforcing harmful racist tropes. The meme is hateful as it targets an individual based on her race and uses degrading imagery to attack her identity and worth.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_025eb6ee"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
